BCC_Q({"lv": "910", "y": 2025, "n": 5, "part": "A", "topic": "ds", "title": "Favourite Fruit", "answer": 3, "story": "<p>Apples <img alt=\"\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:0.31667in; vertical-align:bottom;\"/>, bananas <img alt=\"\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:0.51667in; vertical-align:bottom;\"/> and pears <img alt=\"\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:0.31667in; vertical-align:bottom;\"/> are placed in five baskets so that each basket has eight pieces of fruit.<\/p>\n<p>Given any two baskets, Blake always prefers the basket with more\napples. If two baskets have the same number of apples, then Blake\nprefers the basket with more bananas.<\/p>", "question": "<p>Which of the following shows the five baskets ordered from Blake's\nmost preferred to least preferred from left to right?<\/p>\n<ol class=\"mc\">\n<li> <img alt=\"From left to right the baskets have the following: \n5 apples, 0 bananas, and 3 pears; \n3 apples, 2 bananas, and 3 pears; \n3 apples, 4 bananas, and 1 pear; \n2 apples, 4 bananas, and 2 pears;\n1 apple, 3 bananas, and 4 pears.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:6.94444in; vertical-align:middle;\"/> <\/li>\n<li> <img alt=\"3 apples, 4 bananas, and 1 pear; \n2 apples, 4 bananas, and 2 pears;\n1 apple, 3 bananas, and 4 pears;\n3 apples, 2 bananas, and 3 pears; \n5 apples, 0 bananas, and 3 pears;\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:6.94444in; vertical-align:middle;\"/> <\/li>\n<li> <img alt=\"1 apple, 3 bananas, and 4 pears;\n3 apples, 2 bananas, and 3 pears; \n5 apples, 0 bananas, and 3 pears; \n2 apples, 4 bananas, and 2 pears;\n3 apples, 4 bananas, and 1 pear; \" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:6.94444in; vertical-align:middle;\"/> <\/li>\n<li> <img alt=\"5 apples, 0 bananas, and 3 pears; \n3 apples, 4 bananas, and 1 pear;\n3 apples, 2 bananas, and 3 pears;  \n2 apples, 4 bananas, and 2 pears;\n1 apple, 3 bananas, and 4 pears.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:6.94444in; vertical-align:middle;\"/> <\/li>\n<\/ol>", "answerHtml": "<p>(D) <img alt=\"5 apples, 0 bananas, and 3 pears; \n3 apples, 4 bananas, and 1 pear;\n3 apples, 2 bananas, and 3 pears;  \n2 apples, 4 bananas, and 2 pears;\n1 apple, 3 bananas, and 4 pears.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:6.94444in; vertical-align:middle;\"/> <\/p>", "explanation": "<p>In Option D, the number of apples in the baskets from left to right\nis 5, 3, 3, 2, 1. Of the two baskets with 3 apples, the basket with 4\nbananas comes before the basket with 2 bananas. Therefore, this option\nshows the baskets ordered from Blake's most preferred to least\npreferred.<\/p>\n<p>Option A is incorrect because the two baskets with 3 apples are out\nof order. That is, the basket with 2 bananas comes before the basket\nwith 4 bananas.<\/p>\n<p>Options B and C are incorrect because the basket with the most apples\nis not first.<\/p>", "connections": ""});